# DESCRIPTION

k1-gpio drives the SpacemiT K1's GPIO controller, at `0xd4019000`: 128 GPIOs in four banks of 32, each bank's registers at its own offset (0, 4, 8 and 0x100).
devmgr(8) starts it after the APBC's k1-syscon(3), whose clocks it turns on, and before the devices that link to it, by its record:

```text
driver k1-gpio
class gpio
match dt spacemit,k1-gpio
```

A device's `gpios` or `<name>-gpios` names the controller and three cells, the bank, the pin in it and flags, bit 0 active low: GPIO 116 is `3 20 0`.
devmgr gives the controller's tree to that device's driver at `/dev/provider/<service>`, and its `/dev/dt/links` gives the cells, as regulator-fixed(3)'s does.
An output is set to its level through the bank's set or clear register before it is made an output, so it never drives the other level.
A watched pin's rising and falling edges are latched in its bank's edge status, and its bit in the bank's mask lets them raise the controller's one interrupt, PLIC 58, which devmgr grants.
The driver serves it on a thread of its own, and every 50 ms against a lost one: it reads every bank's edge status, clears every edge it finds, a watched pin's or not, and counts one for each watched pin that had one.
At start no pin's edges are enabled or let through, and none is pending.
A pin's edges stay enabled while the interrupt is served, so none is lost; two close together may be counted as one.

# FILES

The tree is served in devmgr(8)'s, at `drivers/k1-gpio-gpio@d4019000`, and at `/dev/provider/<service>` in the drivers of the devices that link to it.

: `ctl`
  Takes a command a line, `gpio <bank> <pin> <flags> on|off|input|watch`: the pin driven to its active level, to the other, made an input, or watched for edges, numbers in decimal or `0x` hexadecimal.
  `watch` leaves the pin's direction as it is; watched again, a pin takes the new flags.
  A line it can't parse, a pin it doesn't have, or a `watch` with no interrupt to serve it fails the write as invalid, and the driver logs which.
: `events`
  Read only.
  A line for each watched pin, `gpio <bank> <pin> <flags> active|inactive edges <n>`, its level now and the interrupts that found an edge on it; `none` with none watched.
  A channel's first read answers at once; each later one waits until the text differs from what that channel read last, after an edge on a watched pin or another pin watched, as sdhci(3) reads its card detect.
: `status`
  Read only.
  `gpios 128, banks 4`; then a line for each bank as its registers read now, `bank 3 outputs 0x00100000 levels 0x00100000 watched 0x00000000`, a bit a pin; then `commands <n>, failed <n>`, `last failure: <command>: <why>`, and `interrupts <n> polls <n>`, or `no interrupt: no line can be watched` where devmgr granted none.

